      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Consider the two sets of $6$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $22$ | $24$ | $25$ | $23$ | $21$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $13$ | $15$ | $16$ | $18$ | $14$ | $17$ |\n\nCalculate ${S}_{yy}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ ${S}_{yy}$ is the sum of the squared deviations of the data ${y}_{i}$ from the mean $\\overset{―}{y},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{yy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample mean $\\overset{―}{y}:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{13+15+16+18+14+17}{6}=15.5\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the ${y}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}$, and their squares.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $22$ | $24$ | $25$ | $23$ | $21$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $13$ | $15$ | $16$ | $18$ | $14$ | $17$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})\\,$** | $-2.5$ | $-0.5$ | $0.5$ | $2.5$ | $-1.5$ | $1.5$ |\n| **$\\,({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y})^{2}\\,$** | $6.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $6.25$ | $2.25$ | $2.25$ |\n\nTherefore, ${S}_{yy}$ is\n\n$$\n{S}_{yy}=6.25+0.25+0.25+6.25+2.25+2.25=17.5.\n$$",
